WEBVTT

0
00:00:02.809 --> 00:00:03.230
Hello,

1
00:00:03.849 --> 00:00:07.750
the California Department of Motor Vehicles has a unique unit that focuses

2
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.350
on the needs and concerns of senior drivers and their families.

3
00:00:11.569 --> 00:00:14.689
It's called the Senior Driver Ombudsman and Outreach Unit,

4
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:18.239
and it's staffed with dedicated DMV representatives who are

5
00:00:18.239 --> 00:00:22.879
committed to helping senior drivers maintain their driving independence.

6
00:00:23.209 --> 00:00:24.079
After all,

7
00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:24.870
we know

8
00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.709
that mobility matters.

9
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.309
Our team makes sure that senior drivers are treated with dignity,

10
00:00:30.709 --> 00:00:30.969
respect,

11
00:00:31.229 --> 00:00:32.209
and fairly

12
00:00:32.389 --> 00:00:34.729
consistent with our laws and regulations.

13
00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:39.529
We do that by offering outreach seminars for large and small audiences.

14
00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:43.090
I'll be providing you with some contact numbers in just a little bit.

15
00:00:43.549 --> 00:00:47.580
Our team also assists with individual cases that deal with public safety,

16
00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.610
sort of a go-between to resolve DMV issues.

17
00:00:51.159 --> 00:00:54.970
We want to keep seniors driving for as long as they can do so safely.

18
00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:55.909
In fact,

19
00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:59.000
research has shown that senior drivers are some of

20
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.709
the safest drivers on our roads and highways.

21
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.779
California law requires drivers who are 70 years of age or older

22
00:01:05.959 --> 00:01:09.360
to renew their driver's license in person when it expires.

23
00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.819
Here's what you can expect when you visit a DMV office.

24
00:01:13.199 --> 00:01:16.699
You'll need to take a short 18 question driver knowledge exam,

25
00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.660
pass a vision examination.

26
00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:21.739
And have a new picture taken for your driver's license.

27
00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.879
You'll have to repeat this process every 5 years.

28
00:01:25.139 --> 00:01:25.519
Again,

29
00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.800
this is a state law and not a DMV mandate.

30
00:01:29.379 --> 00:01:30.699
We know that as we get older,

31
00:01:30.819 --> 00:01:34.839
our reflexes slow down and we may experience issues with our vision.

32
00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.120
These types of physical changes can put you and other drivers at risk.

33
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.379
If you find yourself in this position.

34
00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:44.800
You may be asked to come back to our office for a re-examination.

35
00:01:45.779 --> 00:01:46.169
Generally,

36
00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.050
law enforcement,

37
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.370
medical professionals,

38
00:01:48.699 --> 00:01:51.349
family and friends submit these types of requests.

39
00:01:51.709 --> 00:01:55.300
The DMV then investigates to evaluate your level of risk.

40
00:01:55.699 --> 00:01:58.419
You also may be asked to provide medical information

41
00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.279
and take a knowledge exam and a driving test.

42
00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:02.010
Now,

43
00:02:02.019 --> 00:02:04.569
if your medical condition impacts your mobility,

44
00:02:04.819 --> 00:02:08.320
you may be able to apply for a disabled person parking placard.

45
00:02:08.788 --> 00:02:11.710
They're available to both drivers and passengers,

46
00:02:11.949 --> 00:02:16.529
and they can only be used when the person to whom it's assigned is inside the vehicle.

47
00:02:17.229 --> 00:02:21.529
That means it's illegal to lend it to a family member or a friend,

48
00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.179
use someone else's,

49
00:02:23.389 --> 00:02:26.529
or alter a placard or placard identification card.

50
00:02:27.029 --> 00:02:28.369
To request a placard,

51
00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:29.929
you need to complete an application.

52
00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.649
Which includes a section that requires a

53
00:02:32.649 --> 00:02:35.539
licensed medical professional to complete and sign.

54
00:02:35.779 --> 00:02:38.779
These placards are honored in all 50 states.

55
00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:39.759
Right now,

56
00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:43.490
permanent placards are automatically renewed every 2 years,

57
00:02:43.619 --> 00:02:45.820
but beginning in June 2023,

58
00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:50.240
placard holders will need to submit a renewal notice every 6 years.

59
00:02:50.449 --> 00:02:52.699
A medical certification is not required.

60
00:02:52.845 --> 00:02:53.365
Required.

61
00:02:53.604 --> 00:02:57.595
Temporary placards are also available and valid up to 6 months.

62
00:02:57.764 --> 00:03:00.705
You can find more information on the DMV website

63
00:03:00.845 --> 00:03:04.044
at DMV.C.gov.

64
00:03:04.565 --> 00:03:05.184
Overall,

65
00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:07.675
seniors are responsible drivers.

66
00:03:07.964 --> 00:03:10.304
They're constantly monitoring their health,

67
00:03:10.485 --> 00:03:12.285
assessing their driving abilities,

68
00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:15.065
and evaluating when it's time to stop driving.

69
00:03:15.699 --> 00:03:19.839
We recommend that seniors discuss this transition with family and friends

70
00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.399
and develop a plan

71
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.919
on how to move around and remain as independent as possible.

72
00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.399
There are several options you should investigate.

73
00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:31.399
You may want to find out if there's a paratransit service in your area,

74
00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:34.919
identify public transportation and ride share companies.

75
00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.059
Reach out to senior centers

76
00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.320
and check if family and friends may be able to offer you a lift.

77
00:03:41.229 --> 00:03:45.649
Don't forget that many grocery stores and pharmacies offer delivery service,

78
00:03:46.389 --> 00:03:47.770
medications can be ordered by mail,

79
00:03:48.039 --> 00:03:50.250
and you can also shop online.

80
00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:52.589
Now if you're concerned about the driving ability

81
00:03:52.589 --> 00:03:55.050
of a family member or someone you know,

82
00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:58.729
it's very important to approach this issue with compassion.

83
00:03:59.149 --> 00:04:01.630
Now you may feel frustrated and even guilty

84
00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.250
about depriving someone of their freedom to drive,

85
00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.850
but remain positive

86
00:04:06.029 --> 00:04:07.059
and supportive.

87
00:04:07.669 --> 00:04:09.740
Older drivers may think that authorities,

88
00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:10.470
friends,

89
00:04:10.509 --> 00:04:12.330
or relatives are out to get them,

90
00:04:12.589 --> 00:04:14.270
and that's why it's important to be

91
00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:17.040
sensitive about how you start this conversation.

92
00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:18.329
And remember,

93
00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:22.890
age alone should not be a basis for limiting someone's driving privilege

94
00:04:23.149 --> 00:04:24.570
or taking it away.

95
00:04:24.829 --> 00:04:28.630
You can find more information in the DMV senior guide for safe driving,

96
00:04:28.709 --> 00:04:30.769
which is available on our website,

97
00:04:30.989 --> 00:04:33.190
DMV.C.gov.

98
00:04:33.829 --> 00:04:38.209
We also offer video tutorials to help you brush up on your driving skills.

99
00:04:38.489 --> 00:04:42.190
Just click the YouTube icon that you find at the bottom of our home page.

100
00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:44.529
Here are some other helpful resources.

101
00:04:44.829 --> 00:04:47.609
AARP offers a mature driving program.

102
00:04:47.989 --> 00:04:48.750
AAA

103
00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:50.329
has a car fit program

104
00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.750
to help your personal vehicle fit you better,

105
00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:57.390
and you may want to check with the CHP about its Drive Smart classes.

106
00:04:57.589 --> 00:04:58.869
And as promised earlier,

107
00:04:59.059 --> 00:05:03.230
here's how you can contact our DMV senior driver ombudsman and outreach unit.

108
00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.290
If you live in Southern California,

109
00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:09.839
call 310-615-3552.

110
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:11.519
In Northern California,

111
00:05:11.709 --> 00:05:16.829
the number is 916-657-6464.

112
00:05:17.369 --> 00:05:21.380
DME representatives are available to participate in outreach seminars

113
00:05:21.489 --> 00:05:23.869
to promote driver safety in California

114
00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:24.989
with an emphasis

115
00:05:25.239 --> 00:05:26.750
on senior concerns.

116
00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:28.869
Did you know by the year 2030,

117
00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:33.640
an estimated 1 in 5 drivers in the United States will be 65 years or older?

118
00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:34.010
Well,

119
00:05:34.089 --> 00:05:37.589
that's why the California DMV will continue to work with our seniors

120
00:05:37.809 --> 00:05:42.549
to maintain their driving independence for as long as they can do so safely.